<title>GERMANY: German chemicals see 1997 growth under two pct.</title>
<headline>German chemicals see 1997 growth under two pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German chemical industry is unlikely to grow more than two percent in 1997, the chairman of the German chemical association (VCI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Forecasts of more than two percent production growth for the German chemical industry in 1997 are really on the optimistic side,&quot; Juergen Strube, head of chemical firm BASF, told a press conference at a VCI meeting.</p>
<p>Earlier on Thursday the VCI said it expected a drop of one percent in sales for the whole of 1996 and a rise of one percent in production.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
